# Research article template of a journal: the document documents/examples/swift-nest-bricks with Slots for the
# article. The journal, its layout, the running head and the folio, the abstract box and the closing Acknowledgements
# and References are part of the template; the article comes in the data: its metadata, the volume, year and pages of
# the issue, the title, the authors and their affiliations (with their superscript marks), the abstract, the sections,
# the acknowledgements, the references and the footnotes. Each section has its parts, and each part an optional
# subsection heading, its paragraphs, its figures (each one with a table or an image) and a list of findings; the texts
# are Markdown, with the citations and cross-references of the document ({number of: id}). swift-nest-bricks.json has
# the sample data.
# The title, the authors and the abstract go across the page and the body in two Columns, where the headings, the
# figures and the table flow from one column to the next. The sections are numbered headings (Numbered: 1, 2, 2.1...),
# and the running head of every page but the first is the section in effect ({heading 1: first}, the first section
# that starts on the page, in a Page overlay with Pages: not-first). The figures and the table have numbered captions
# ("Figure 1.", "Table 1.") that the text cites with {number of: id} and {page of: id}, the citations are the numbers
# of the items of the reference list ([{number of: ref-id}], each one a link to its item) and the footnotes sit at the
# bottom of the page of their call. The affiliation marks are superscript styled runs ([1]{sup}, Position:
# superscript). Hyphenation in US English and optimal line breaking give the justified columns an even colour.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Page:
		Paper: A4
		Margin: 24mm 18mm 22mm 18mm
	Title: <title>
	Subject: <subject>
	Author: <author>
	Keywords: <keywords>
	Language: en-US
	Page overlay:
		Id: running-head
		Pages: not-first
		Offset: -14mm 0 auto 0
		Style: running-head
		Stack:
			Horizontal: justify
			Item:
				Text: ${short_authors} · ${short_title}
			Item:
				Text: {heading 1: first}
	Page overlay:
		Id: folio
		Offset: auto 0 -13mm 0
		Style: folio
		Stack:
			Horizontal: justify
			Item:
				Text: Urban Ecology Notes ${volume} (${year}) ${page_range}
			Item:
				# A value that starts with {page} would be the navigation {page}: the empty ${?_} in front, which no
				# data fills, makes the whole value text.
				Text: ${?_}{page}
	Section:
		Page numbering: restart
		First number: <first_page>
		Block:
			Id: front
			Text: Urban Ecology Notes · ${type}
				Style: journal
			Heading 1:
				Id: title
				Style: paper-title
				In table of contents: false
				Text: ${title}
			Paragraph: <authors>
				Style: authors
			Paragraph: ${affiliations} · Correspondence: [${email}](mailto:${email})
				Style: affiliations
			Block: {abstract}
				Style: abstract
				Text: Abstract
					Style: abstract-label
				Paragraph: <text>
				Paragraph: **Keywords:** ${keywords}
					Style: keywords
		Columns:
			Id: body
			Style: body
			# Each section is a Block with its heading and its parts, and each part (a subsection, or the paragraphs and
			# figures between two figures) is another Block. They have no box of their own.
			Block: [sections]
				Heading 1:
					Id: <id>
					Text: <title>
				Block: [parts]
					Heading 2: {?subsection}
						Id: <id>
						Text: <title>
					Paragraph: [?paragraphs]
					Figure: [?figures]
						Id: <id>
						Caption: <caption>
						Table: {?table}
							Style: data
							Header rows:
								Row:
									Cell: [columns]
							Body rows:
								Row: [rows]
									Cell: <name>
										Row header: true
									Cell: [values]
							Footer rows: {?total}
								Row:
									Cell: <name>
										Row header: true
									Cell: [values]
						Image: <?image>
							Alt: <alt>
							Box:
								Width: 100%
					List: {?findings}
						Style: findings
						List item: [items]
							Paragraph: <text>
			Heading 1:
				Id: acknowledgements
				Style: unnumbered
				Text: Acknowledgements
			Paragraph: <acknowledgements>
			Heading 1:
				Id: references
				Style: unnumbered
				Text: References
			List:
				Style: references
				List item: [references]
					Id: <id>
					Paragraph: <text>
			# The footnotes, each one called from the text with [^id].
			Footnote: [footnotes]
				Id: <id>
				Paragraph: <text>
